    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0142" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862R.014/9–2646: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-26T12:00:00+01:00">September 26,
                        1946—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 9:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4819. Department’s 5049, September 24.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d77-f1"/> We
                    explained to Chauvel<anchor n="11" xml:id="d77-f2"/> the U.S. attitude regarding
                    proposed annexation Southwest Africa which Union has placed on UNO agenda. He replied that our proposal would have
                    to be studied before he could give us an official reply but to him personally it
                    appeared “very reasonable”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d77-f1" n="10" xml:id="d77-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d77-f2" n="11" xml:id="d77-f2-content">
                <p>Jean Chauvel, Secretary General of the French Ministry of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
